CM LPDA
CM
CM 
CM LPDA.nc
CM Doug Hall K4DSP
CM June 4, 2009
CM 
CM LPDA.nc models a Log Periodic Dipole Array. Set the variables below for the number
CM of elements, the boom length, the min and max frequencies, and the height. The program
CM uses a recursive function to create the elements of the antenna and connects them with
CM a crossed transmission line.
CM 
CM This is a simplistic model. The usual LPDA calculation of Tau, Sigma, and Alpha is not
CM performed. Instead, the elements are equally spaced on the boom, and the difference in
CM length from one element to the next is a constant.
CE
SY numElements=8
SY boom=18ft
SY lowestfreq=13.0 ! MHz
! MHz
SY highestfreq=30.0 ! MHz
! MHz
SY height=50ft
! calculate the amount to shorten each successive element
SY eledelta=((492/lowestfreq)-(492/highestfreq))/(numElements-1)
SY eledelta=eledelta*0.305
SY eledelta=eledelta/2.0
! Calculate space between each element. Elements are equally spaced on the boom.
SY boomdelta=boom/(numElements-1)
! calculate longest and shortest elements
SY longelement=(492/lowestfreq)*0.305
SY shortelement=(492/highestfreq)*0.305
SY wirex=0 ! start at one end of the boom
! start at one end of the boom
SY wirey=longelement/2
GE 0
GN -1
FR 0,1,0,0,14,0
RP 0,37,73,1000,0,0,5,5
EN
